@node API
@chapter API

@cindex API
@vindex restlib

To use @strong{restlib}@comma{} include it in your code using the @code{require} function:

@lisp
(require 'restlib)
@end lisp


The @strong{restlib} library is organized into sections listed below:

@menu
* Network::
* URL Components::
* JSON::
@end menu

@node Network
@section Network

@vindex restlib-fetch-json

Network-related functions.

@defun restlib-fetch-json URL
@itemize
@item
URL: string or URL object
@end itemize

Synchronously fetch the URL returning a deserialized JSON response.

The following is done with a URL whose response is in JSON:

@enumerate
@item
Synchronously fetch the URL@.

@item
Upon success@comma{} deserialize the JSON into an Elisp @code{hash-table}@comma{} with JSON null values converted to nil.

@item
Return the JSON @code{hash-table} object.
@end enumerate

Any failure in the HTTP request will raise an @code{error} message. Refer to Emacs Lisp Reference Manual for guidance on handling this condition (@ref{Handling Errors,,,elisp,}).

Example:

@lisp
(restlib-fetch-json "https://wttr.in/?0&format=j1")
@end lisp
@end defun

@node URL Components
@section URL Components

@vindex restlib-url-parse
@vindex restlib-url-filename
@vindex restlib-url-path
@vindex restlib-url-query
@vindex restlib-url-query-items
@vindex restlib-url-add-query-items
@vindex restlib-url-remove-query

URL-related functions. For more information on URL objects refer to the @ref{Top,URL manual,,url,}.

@defun restlib-url-parse URL
@itemize
@item
URL: string or URL object
@end itemize

Convenience function to return a parsed object given URL string.

If the URL is already a parsed object then it will pass through.
@end defun

@defun restlib-url-filename URL
@itemize
@item
URL: string or URL object
@end itemize

Get URL filename.

Extract filename via @code{url-filename}.

Example:

@lisp
(restlib-url-filename "https://heythey.com/mary?a=b&c=d%2Ce")
@end lisp

Result:

@example
"/mary?a=b&c=d%2Ce"
@end example
@end defun

@defun restlib-url-path URL
@itemize
@item
URL: string or URL object
@end itemize

Get URL path.

Extract only path from URL@comma{} omitting query parameters and fragment.

Example:

@lisp
(restlib-url-path "https://heythey.com/mary?a=b&c=d%2Ce")
@end lisp

Result:

@example
"/mary"
@end example
@end defun

@defun restlib-url-query URL
@itemize
@item
URL: string or URL object
@end itemize

Get URL query.

Extract query as string from URL@.

Example:

@lisp
(restlib-url-query "https://heythey.com/mary?a=b&c=d%2Ce")
@end lisp

Result:

@example
"a=b&c=d%20e"
@end example
@end defun

@defun restlib-url-query-items URL
@itemize
@item
URL: string or URL object
@end itemize

Extract query items from URL@.

Extract query items using @code{url-parse-query-string}.

Example:

@lisp
(restlib-url-query-items "https://heythey.com/mary?a=b&c=d%2Ce")
@end lisp

Result:

@example
(("c" "d@comma{}e") ("a" "b"))
@end example
@end defun

@defun restlib-url-add-query-items URL ITEMS &optional OBJ-RESULT SEMICOLONS KEEP-EMPTY
@itemize
@item
URL: string or URL object
@item
ITEMS: list of lists as specified for @code{url-build-query-string}
@item
OBJ-RESULT: if non-nil then return URL object@comma{} else string
@item
SEMICOLONS: if non-nil then use ‘;’ as separator
@item
KEEP-EMPTY: if non-nil then render ‘key=’ instead of ‘key’
@end itemize

Add query ITEMS to URL@.

If URL has an existing query fragment@comma{} then ITEMS will be naively appended to it@comma{} with no regard for duplicate keys.

Example:

@lisp
(restlib-url-add-query-items
 "https://heythey.com/mary?a=b&c=d%2Ce"
 '(("f" "j")))
@end lisp

Result:

@example
"https://heythey.com/mary?c=d@comma{}e&a=b&f=j"
@end example
@end defun

@defun restlib-url-remove-query URL &optional OBJ-RESULT
@itemize
@item
URL: string or URL object
@item
OBJ-RESULT: if non-nil then return URL object
@end itemize

Remove query from URL@.

Example:

@lisp
(restlib-url-remove-query "https://heythey.com/mary?a=b&c=d%2Ce")
@end lisp

Result:

@example
"https://heythey.com/mary"
@end example
@end defun

@node JSON
@section JSON

@vindex restlib-json-empty-string-to-nil

JSON-related functions. For more information on JSON objects@comma{} refer to the @ref{Parsing JSON,Parsing JSON section of the Elisp manual,,elisp,}.

@defun restlib-json-empty-string-to-nil OBJ KEY
@itemize
@item
OBJ: map-type object (typically a @code{hash-table})
@item
KEY: key
@end itemize

Convert empty string value for KEY to nil in OBJ@.
@end defun

